ult.\n\n```python\n# Calculate the number of valid (x, y) pairs\ndef count_triangles():\n    count = 0\n    for x in range(1, 55, 2):\n        y = (2023 - 37 * x) // 2\n        if y >= 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\n# Final number of such triangles\nprint(count_triangles())\n```\n```output\n27\n```\nThe number of distinct triangles \\(ORQ\\) whose perimeter is a positive integer is \\(\\boxed{27}\\).",
